From 920c69bdcac38de8ece0c0dc5b5bea0276506ee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:28:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] graphical_debug: scrolling, scaled, coloured boot
 console

Keep a shadow cell grid so the console scrolls instead of wrapping to
the top, redrawing only cells that change and never reading framebuffer
memory. Scale the 8x16 font by min(width, height) / 540 (2x on the
OnePlus 6's 1080x2280 panel), clear to black, draw the logger prefix in
orange and the message in white, and whole WARN/ERROR/PANIC lines in
orange. Optionally clean written lines to the point of coherency, for
the bootloader mapping that may be cacheable before the kernel's own
write-combining map exists.

Host tests render into a framebuffer model: a golden 'K' cell, every
printable glyph against the font, colours, scrolling, wrapping, escape
handling, untouched stride padding, 2x scaling and grid clamping.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
